{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 995016,
  "courseSlug": "vuejs-2-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Vue - The Complete Guide (incl. Router & Composition API)",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21879354",
      "title": "Passing Params as Props",
      "lectureOrder": 178,
      "videoOrder": 154,
      "sourceHash": "37e820dad7f7e3eed611ac11d7466127e623652b81ab4870809acedbacdd4840",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.21,
          "end": 6.68,
          "en": "Our TeamMembers component has one potential disadvantage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 6.68,
          "end": 10.593,
          "en": "It's not only loadable through routing, why?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 11.57,
          "end": 12.96,
          "en": "Because in the code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.96,
          "end": 16.68,
          "en": "we rely on $route in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 16.68,
          "end": 20.02,
          "en": "we use it here in created and we watch it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 20.02,
          "end": 24.04,
          "en": "So if you would use this component by simply embedding it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 24.04,
          "end": 26.32,
          "en": "in the template of another component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.32,
          "end": 28.22,
          "en": "let's say you change your application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.22,
          "end": 30.59,
          "en": "and you now suddenly want to use this differently,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.59,
          "end": 32.58,
          "en": "or you use it in different places,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.58,
          "end": 34.444,
          "en": "one time loaded through routing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.444,
          "end": 37.89,
          "en": "another time used through its tag in the template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.89,
          "end": 40.44,
          "en": "then this would be problematic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.44,
          "end": 44.58,
          "en": "It might be better if TeamMembers would be loaded such",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.58,
          "end": 47.21,
          "en": "that you get props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.21,
          "end": 50.42,
          "en": "that you simply get your",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.42,
          "end": 52.373,
          "en": "teamId as a prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.42,
          "end": 55.53,
          "en": "That's how you would build this component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.53,
          "end": 57.82,
          "en": "if it would not be loaded through routing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 57.82,
          "end": 60.4,
          "en": "You would get the teamId through props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.24,
          "end": 63.31,
          "en": "and in all the places where you need the Id,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 63.31,
          "end": 65.37,
          "en": "instead of using this $route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 65.37,
          "end": 70.05,
          "en": "you use this teamId, referring to that prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.05,
          "end": 71.85,
          "en": "and here, you could then watch this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 71.85,
          "end": 73.853,
          "en": "prop for a changes, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 74.75,
          "end": 77.03999999999999,
          "en": "And then we would get our newId here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 77.03999999999999,
          "end": 80.247,
          "en": "would maybe forward that to LoadMembers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 80.247,
          "end": 83.21000000000001,
          "en": "And we will change the LoadMembers code here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 83.21000000000001,
          "end": 87.12,
          "en": "to not expect the route as argument but the teamId,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 87.12,
          "end": 91.2,
          "en": "and therefore, we now just got teamId as an argument here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 91.2,
          "end": 93.363,
          "en": "and we can delete that old first line.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 94.55,
          "end": 96.1,
          "en": "But if we save that it won't work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 96.1,
          "end": 99.49000000000001,
          "en": "we see nothing on the screen /t2",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 99.49000000000001,
          "end": 101.25999999999999,
          "en": "and if we open the developer tools,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 101.25999999999999,
          "end": 102.72999999999999,
          "en": "we see that the problem is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 102.72999999999999,
          "end": 106.71000000000001,
          "en": "that we cannot read the property 'members' of undefined.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 106.71000000000001,
          "end": 108.19,
          "en": "And the reason should be obvious,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 108.19,
          "end": 110.45,
          "en": "teamId is expected as a prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 110.45,
          "end": 112.45,
          "en": "but we're loading this through routing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 112.45,
          "end": 115.08,
          "en": "and the router by default doesn't add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 115.08,
          "end": 117.93299999999999,
          "en": "any props to this loaded component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 119.15,
          "end": 121.36,
          "en": "but that's something you can change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 121.36,
          "end": 124.5,
          "en": "In your route config, here on this route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 124.5,
          "end": 126.32,
          "en": "which is the route responsible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 126.32,
          "end": 128.57,
          "en": "for loading the TeamMembers component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 128.57,
          "end": 131.07,
          "en": "you can add another option,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 131.07,
          "end": 135.31,
          "en": "you can add the props option and set this to true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 135.31,
          "end": 137.43,
          "en": "And this does one important thing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 137.43,
          "end": 142.43,
          "en": "it tells the view router that the dynamic parameters",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 142.61,
          "end": 145.65,
          "en": "should be passed into this component as props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 145.65,
          "end": 149.523,
          "en": "rather than just on the $route property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 150.63,
          "end": 153.38,
          "en": "So now, you will have a prop off the name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 153.38,
          "end": 155.38,
          "en": "you defined here after the colon,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 155.38,
          "end": 159.99,
          "en": "in my case, teamId, the value which is now part of the URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 159.99,
          "end": 163.7,
          "en": "will now be passed in as a prop into this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 163.7,
          "end": 164.55,
          "en": "when it's loaded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 165.68,
          "end": 170.68,
          "en": "So with props true if you save that and reload now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 171.04,
          "end": 173.01,
          "en": "this works again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 173.01,
          "end": 175.21,
          "en": "And now we have one advantage,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 175.21,
          "end": 180.21,
          "en": "now, this component TeamMembers is more reusable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 180.32,
          "end": 182.23,
          "en": "because now we can use it anywhere,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 182.23,
          "end": 184.46,
          "en": "as long as we provide this prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 184.46,
          "end": 187.723,
          "en": "it's not strictly tied to routing anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 188.57,
          "end": 191.31,
          "en": "So this is simply an alternative,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 191.31,
          "end": 194.75,
          "en": "which you could consider when it comes to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 194.75,
          "end": 198.16,
          "en": "routing and loading components through routing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 198.16,
          "end": 201.05,
          "en": "You can make your components more reusable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 201.05,
          "end": 204.02,
          "en": "by using props instead of $route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 204.02,
          "end": 205.75,
          "en": "and even if you don't plan",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 205.75,
          "end": 207.76,
          "en": "on using the component anywhere else?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 207.76,
          "end": 210.97,
          "en": "You might prefer getting your data through props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 210.97,
          "end": 213.01,
          "en": "than having to search for it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 213.01,
          "end": 215.513,
          "en": "in the $route parents property.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
